Well, we kind of need both.  The focus of this system is teaching/learning rather than just testing.  The fundamental notion is that it is unfair to expect a learner know how to do something without having been given direct
 instruction beforehand.  I want students to come away able not only to code solutions to questions - definitely an "implement a function" focus - but also with the ability to write and run their own little programs.  Depending on the learning goals.

